# text = We're their slaves as long as we can work ; we pile up their fortunes with the sweat of our brows , and yet we are to live as separate as if we were in two worlds ; ay , as separate as Dives and Lazarus , with a great gulf betwixt us : but I know who was best off then Well , neighbour all that may be very true , but what I want to know now is about Esther -- when did you last hear of her Why , she took leave of us that Sunday night in a very loving way , kissing both wife Mary , and daughter Mary ( if I must not call her ' little '), and shaking hands with me ; but all in a cheerful sort of manner , so we thought nothing about her kisses and shakes .
