# text = We've not proud nor soaring wings , Our ambition , our content , Lies in simple things ; Humble voyagers are we O'er life's dim unsounded sea ; Touch us gently , gentle Time To be sure ' Merica is a long way to flit to ; beyond London a good bit I reckon ; and quite in foreign parts ; but I've never had no opinion of England , ever since they could be such fools as to take up a quiet chap like thee , and clap thee in prison .
